;; repr/haskell's known differences at the text level over the corpus ghc-9.14.1 (doc/haskell/SPEC.md
;; §9.1, §9.5; bin/repr-haskell roundtrip --text, milestone R3): a map from PKG/FILE to the reason
;; the module differs, read with the Clojure reader: its printed text against its original (a CPP
;; module's: its module view, SPEC §2.8), then GHC's trees and lines in mode :full (hsdump tree
;; --full) of both. The round trip fails on a module that differs and is not listed, and on a
;; listed one that no longer differs. R3 (2026-10-17): every module's text is byte-identical; the
;; three modules that #include "CTypes.h", a header with Haskell comments, differ in GHC's trees of
;; mode :full only: the original's tree holds the header's comments (spans in include/CTypes.h),
;; which the module view leaves out with the header's other lines (S5), so GHC attaches the
;; module's own documentation comment before the inclusion elsewhere. R5 (2026-10-17): the 12
;; modules whose nodes are in another file (doc/haskell/HASKELL-NOTES.md, R5, HR18) do not convert
;; in mode :full: 11 #include another file's Haskell source (filepath's Internal.hs and
;; OsPath/Common.hs, os-string's Common.hs, bytestring's Lazy/ReadInt.hs, Lazy/ReadNat.hs), which
;; the module view (SPEC §2.8, S5) leaves out, and the alex output Lexer.hs names its lines
;; Lexer.x's with {-# LINE #-} pragmas, whose tokens the helper's token stream leaves out with
;; other files'; mode :lines converts all of them (the tree, layout and interface levels). R6
;; (2026-10-18): the three .hsc modules whose hsc2hs output keeps CPP directives (an #include, #if)
;; differ in GHC's trees of mode :full only, their texts byte-identical (the output's module view):
;; after a directive CPP's line markers name the output's own lines (X.hs), whereas the module
;; view (SPEC §2.8, S5), which has no directives, stays in the .hsc that hsc2hs's {-# LINE #-}
;; pragmas name, as the CTypes.h modules' (HR12).
